{
  "body": "RF-SR-13 and RF-DEC-07 define a current account with stable finding IDs and editable non-ID fields, no origin/supporting-judgment snapshot or mandatory revision history. Review record/set preserve findings; explicit finding and advanced corrections permit valid current-field changes, while ID removal/rename rejects and withdrawal uses resolved disposition. V2 concerns and v3 blockers retain origin. The approved proposal and earlier review judgments retain their exact historical subjects, not approval of this direction revision. No v3 implementation/adoption or v2 retirement is claimed. Author considers the new rule a proposed correction for design-review-f1; reporter disposition and independent reassessment remain required. design-review-f2 response-version mapping is unchanged and remains open.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-10-structured-assessment-explanations",
  "decisions": [
    {
      "actor": {
        "id": "codex-design-author",
        "role": "design"
      },
      "id": "v3-adoption-and-v2-continuation",
      "rationale": "RF-DEC-06 and the Workflow coordination amendment select v3 for new stores only after coordinated implementation/Verify adoption. Existing-v2 operations and recovery remain available, including this initiative; no automatic conversion or existing-v2 retirement is selected. Removal requires a separately reviewed owner disposition. This avoids stranding the actual in-progress v2 initiative.",
